          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദാമ്പത്യം — dāmpatyaṁ — \"married life\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുത്തച്ഛന്റെയും മുത്തശ്ശിയുടെയും ദാമ്പത്യം അമ്പത് വർഷം നീണ്ടു. muttacchanṟeyuṁ muttaśśiyuṭeyuṁ dāmpatyaṁ ampatŭ varṣaṁ nīṇṭu. My grandparents' married life lasted fifty years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദമ്പതികൾ, a married couple, is already familiar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദാമ്പത്യം (dāmpatyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit dāmpatya, \"the state of husband and wife\" (Monier-Williams), the noun of dampati, \"a married couple\"."
            }
